	spec: 'Normal /sync compares config.ason through an ASON-stringified portable view, reusing history, hashes, diff, review, stale checks and explicit copy choices. Declared settings default to portable: true; webPort and webUrl have portable: false. Unknown keys remain local. Plugins retain opt-in portability. Only portable keys, their existing ASON before-comments and the supported root comment enter the view or transferred history. Non-portable value/comment edits create no sync difference. Preserve insertion order; do not extend ASON or special-case documentation comment text. Review merges both views one setting at a time from the common version (empty without shared history): a value or comment changed on one side takes that change; only different values for the same setting conflict. Applying a reviewed version sets its portable keys and comments in the destination file setting by setting: local settings (webUrl, webPort) first, then portable settings in the incoming order; unknown keys keep their values, comments and neighbors. It uses the existing atomic sync writer; live-file watchers apply the result. This sync write is an exception to the usual live-file write rule. Deletion removes the portable portion only: config.ason is never deleted, including when empty. Empty portable content without a root comment equals absence. Malformed destination files block writes; incompatible incoming non-portable or unknown keys are rejected. Refresh config history from disk before stale checks rather than relying on watcher timing. Invariants: projecting the merged file reproduces the accepted portable version; local-only keys and their supported comments survive; comment-only portable edits are syncable. Keep implementation small with no parallel sync protocol, automatic syncing, parser expansion or key sorting. Tests cover these invariants through ordinary sync and history, both copy directions and deletion.',
